ke it real let's do it  fast  thank you very much mr president we'll  just proceed to the third and  final speaker the prime minister of  poland mr matthews thank you  your floor is yours thank you thank you  mata for organizing this this meeting  let me say a couple of words also about  energy but not only in the context of  energy transformation but maybe even  more focusing on energy security  because we do witness right now  geopolitical shifts  and we don't  know yet um what shape they will  eventually take  therefore we must rely on reliable  partners and so far we were discussing  at length  uh all sorts of different aspects of  energy transformation and we should  do so  in  in in the future as well  but supplementing  those discussions  uh we have to discuss also energy  security because  security overall it's not only about  strong army strong alliance but also  security of um  of  finances of our citizens and also  energy security  which we now so um painfully uh witness  uh as a missing link in our overall  economic and social architecture  russia has  wrapped a web of energy dependency  around europe like a spider  and many countries now have a very hard  time getting out of this  deadly  web  this  the invasion of ukraine is not the only  russian  military operation  the kremlin has been waging a gas and  energy war with europe for years  and this is why all our considerations  around energy uh should be  bearing in mind should bear in mind that  russia is using  energy as a weapon  and this therefore energy security  uh even more important than energy  transformation because there is no  energy transformation without energy  security  for too long the low price of russian  gas or cheap russian gas i should put it  in inverted commas  has been the most important value for  many countries  and the real price for cheap gas today  is the blood  of ukraine  we have learned how risky it is to rely  on unreliable partners as far as energy  issues are concern